      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still don\u0027t understand why this is required? The way it works is:\n1. Power sequencing always starts in chipset_task in power/common.c: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/power/common.c#439\n\n2. Consider we are in G3. Loop in chipset task calls power_handle_state with state \u003d G3. No special action taken within this function. It calls common_intel_x86_power_handle_state at the bottom on line 129 with state \u003d G3.\n\n3. common_intel_x86_power_handle_state takes no action on that and control goes back to chipset_task.\n\n4. chipset_task calls power_common_state next which decides if it should transition to G3S5 based on want_g3_exit. If this is true, state is now set to G3S5.\n\nWhy do you have to force the state to be G3S5 here in icelake specific code?",
